    "text": "<p>For the reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>aA</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>bB</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>cC</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>dD</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the plot of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>&nbsp;v/s <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> is given below:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0114_0b84cb85380f.png\" style=\"width: 226px; height: 174px;\" /></p><p>The temperature at which the rate constant of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />(Rounded-off to the nearest integer) [Given : The rat5e constant of the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>.]</p>"
  },
